WEBVTT

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.980
Huh? You're early. I even came--

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.640
I was curious.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.520
Didn't expect the Insta DM.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.940
Sorry. I made an account
since I don't have your--

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.900
What's this about?

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.990
Right...

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.660
Actually, my memories came back.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.500
But only some. Not everything.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.130
This is... me?

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:52.760
I saw a video of me yelling at the pool.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:59.760
Just then, I got a whiff of chlorine
coming from my hair.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.100
It all came rushing back to me.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.400
Talk about half-assing it!
That pass was pathetic!

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.320
I'm sorry!

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.860
You're giving up shots on goal!
Don't you get it?!

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.700
Hey! I said only to film the games!

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.410
Sorry, Senpai!

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.700
That's all I remember, though.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.330
Hey, do you know what
I was like back then?

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:34.090
I'm afraid to ask my friend,
so I'm hoping you can tell me--

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.970
You finally remember.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:36.840
Huh?

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.510
That's how you really were.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.300
Eh?

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.640
Arrogant, stuck-up, awful...
Making everyone scared of you...

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.520
Huh?

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.860
Do you remember Hiroshi Ichinose?

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.610
I don't.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.280
He was your <i>senpai</i>.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.610
Huh?

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.950
"Chinu Kawakubo"        "Hiroshi Ichinose"

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.950
To me, he was like a brother...
Someone I admired.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:07.120
To me, he was like a brother...
Someone I admired.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.580
He was the reason I picked up water polo.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.880
He always seemed to enjoy it.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:28.180
But his second year, with the new coach
and you joining, he stopped smiling.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.900
And by his third year...

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.360
Dammit!

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.160
Don't let him get by!

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.080
Though his junior,
you were the team's ace.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.210
Are you even trying?
Swim like you actually care!

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.840
And yet, you talked down to him.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.550
Sorry.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.840
Ichinose.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.980
"Water Polo Parent's Association"
"Rikka Gakuen Junior High Water"

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:17.190
In the end, he went to another
school and quit water polo.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.950
That's why I hated you.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.240
Huh?

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.990
And yet, you confessed to me.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.620
No way.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:30.370
When I'm Japan's best water polo player,
you owe me a kiss.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.540
Huh?

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.790
I'll pay you 110,000 yen if I fail. Well?

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.250
That made me hate you more.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:44.050
But you did become the best...
and had the accident.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.140
Then showed up out of nowhere.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.640
You seem better than I thought.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.690
Huh?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.980
I kept the promise, but...

00:03:54.980 --> 00:04:00.530
You said you forgot everything
and wouldn't play water polo.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:03.030
It's hopeless for me.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.120
That pissed me off.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.410
Huh?

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:13.790
Weak players don't last in sports,
so I understand if Ichinose left,

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.790
but I couldn't stand it if you quit, too.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:22.470
I wanted you to take
responsibility by keeping at it.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.050
So, I lied.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.510
Lied?

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.140
You don't remember the other half?

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:31.520
The other half?

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.520
"If I'm Japan's best in high school,
you've gotta date me."

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.940
Huh? That was a lie?

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.490
More like revenge to make
sure you wouldn't quit.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.360
You're kidding!

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:51.370
With or without your memories,
I'll never forgive you if you quit.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.590
Ichinose...

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:12.270
Damn, you totally saved us!

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.390
--Right?
--I stopped #6.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:15.770
I guess.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:18.190
--"I guess"?
--Momo.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:09.380
"Episode 8: Who Are These Guys?"

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.130
"Episode 8: Who Are These Guys?"
"June 13 (Sat)"

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:25.820
Jeez, Kamekichi! I can never
get this part right!

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.820
Jeez!

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.990
Patience, patience.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.750
But the contest is coming up.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.920
July 19th, right?

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.630
It's the 18th.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.170
Huh?

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:46.340
What?

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.510
That day is prefecturals.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.510
What? You mean I can't watch him?!

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.350
Hello?

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.680
Yeah.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.770
What?!

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.100
Can you get home?! You okay?!

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.400
All right.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:13.490
Big Bro... got his memories back.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:20.410
Why'd they come back so suddenly?

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:26.290
After hearing about Ichinose,
my memories just flooded back.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:31.590
My junior high days...
The day of the accident...

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:38.010
I see. It was raining then,
too. Is that why?

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:42.230
I should get home.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.090
Went too far.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.940
"Big Bro"

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:35.240
He's late.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.110
Mmm.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:39.530
Why won't you answer? Jeez...

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:55.220
To think he'd be hospitalized again...
But it's good that he came here.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:58.720
We know his full history.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:03.810
While its effects didn't
manifest in the car accident,

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:09.560
a slight brain wound from then
may have reopened.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.150
Will my brother be okay?

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.070
Physically, yes.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.240
"Kurashiki University Hospital"

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:18.990
"Kurashiki University Hospital"

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:18.990
Here's where it all started,
on July 18th of last year.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:23.540
"3 years"

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:23.540
Here's where it all started,
on July 18th of last year.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.620
"3 years"

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.620
When Minato lost consciousness, he lost
three years of junior-high memories.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:29.540
When Minato lost consciousness, he lost
three years of junior-high memories.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.790
Roughly a year has passed since then.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.380
"1 year"

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.380
Roughly a year has passed since then.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:41.010
This June 13 at 7 P.M., he called saying
his memories had come back.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.470
Yeah.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:49.270
It's likely he remembered these years.
As in, he had regained his full memory.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:57.610
But with this bicycle fall, he hit his
head and lost these memories.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:01.660
Basically, he has memory
loss a second time.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:05.540
Does that even happen?

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:12.460
As I said, it may be a result
from his earlier brain trauma.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:21.090
He's lost memories from this period here--
the last year that he's lived.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.770
Are you doing all right, Big Bro?

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.400
Hardly.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.030
I told her I'm fine,
but the doctor won't listen.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:49.040
And what's with this? Wasn't I just
in Mom's car after the match?

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.040
Well...

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:54.580
Let me tell him.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.670
Minato, listen...

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:06.260
Huh?! I was stuck in bed?
I lost my memories?

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:09.640
That's right. All because
of my accident...

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.100
Bullshit...

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:16.360
That's bullshit!
What'd you do to my life?!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.280
And I just became the best in Japan!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:23.410
Sorry.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.200
I'm sorry.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.920
"2 days later"

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.760
I wonder where he is...

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.010
He didn't come to class.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.310
Catch a cold?

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.810
"You okay?" "Did something happen?"

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.810
"Are you all right?" "Worried about you."
He hasn't even read my messages.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.980
Maybe he overslept or something.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:02.280
That's unforgivable with
the tourney coming up.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.570
Now, now, now.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.800
Kiyomizu!

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.890
Sorry!

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:41.610
"Eat if you can"

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.490
"Strange"

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:52.080
"Strange"

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:52.080
What the hell's that?

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.920
Who are these guys?

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:09.340
Minato...

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.180
Hmm?

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.390
How do we get him to come out?

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:20.110
Patience. Let's let him set
the pace, just like before.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.230
Mmm.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:26.700
He still thinks he's in 6th grade.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:31.450
For now, just let him steer
the conversation.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.410
You okay, Big Bro?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:40.420
Yeah! I'm good! I'm good!

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.550
Welcome.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:51.340
Um, excuse us.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:55.100
We're from Minato's water polo club.

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:01.480
Minato, your friends are here.

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:07.070
Minato? I'm coming in.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.790
"Shogakukan"

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:26.550
"Courtesy of 47th Graduating Class"

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.890
It's been a while.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:41.690
Not for me.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:45.730
I remember everything before the accident.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:47.320
I see.

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:49.570
But nothing from after.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:56.330
It feels like yesterday we were the best
in Japan and you were praising us.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.120
I see.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:08.000
What a shock. I thought I was
in Shogakukan, but now I'm not.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:12.680
I can't believe I'm playing
water polo at Yamanami.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:18.890
I want to play at this school!
Let me back on the team!

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.690
Sorry, but I can't.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.060
Huh?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.690
I can't just enroll you.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:26.820
But--!

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:31.440
And even if I could,
we don't have a place for you.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.320
Follow me.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:44.710
In high school, we train 50% longer.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:49.630
We push their bodies to grow
even more with strength training.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:58.430
You missed over a year of rapid growth.
You can't keep up with our training.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.020
I can do it!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:04.520
While you were growing, they were, too!

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:10.900
The gap has only widened.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:14.900
Momosaki's growth is staggering.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:24.370
He's playing your old position.
There's no place for you now.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:33.630
I'm disappointed, too.
I wanted to see what you grew into.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:49.020
"Kumagaki's Corner"
"Interview with Shogakukan's
water polo star, Riku Momosaki."

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.070
"An Absolute Ace"

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.420
W-Wait!

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:12.500
Don't just ignore us, Minato.

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:15.880
Who are you?

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:19.970
Uh, we're in your water polo club.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:22.010
Ah, Yamanami's...

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:23.140
Yeah!

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:25.020
You remember us?!

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:27.520
Guess not.

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:29.940
I saw a photo of you.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.570
We heard from your parents.

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.860
Sounds rough.

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:36.700
Are you all right?

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:39.990
What do you want? I'm heading home.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:44.740
We came to confirm what your plans are.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.250
Confirm?

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:51.960
You know, we get that it's rough for you,
but next month is our tournament.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.340
When are you coming back?

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.970
Huh? Why would I?

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.430
--Eh?
--Huh?

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:00.800
I'm not playing with you guys.

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:02.390
--Huh?
--What?

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.680
What gives?!

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:08.940
That's what I wanna know.
Why would I ever play with you guys?

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:10.520
We've been playing togeth--

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:14.610
I can't remember and I wouldn't want to.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:16.400
That attitude...

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.150
That's really Minato?

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:20.360
He's another person.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:22.490
It's how he used to be.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:23.580
Huh?

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:25.990
Huh? Aren't you...?

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.250
Ah, yeah! I'm one year below--!

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:33.790
Thought so. You're the one
water polo... Who again?

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:38.170
Eitaro Oka.

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:43.600
Oh, yeah. Oka. You know me,
right? Explain it to them.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:44.640
Huh?

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:47.720
These guys don't have my talent.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:49.020
--Say what?!

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:50.230
--Now, now.
--Say what?!

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.940
Nor taste, either.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:52.730
Eh?!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:58.030
What's with that lame jersey? "Strange"?

00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:02.030
No team worth a damn would wear that.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:04.910
Bye.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.630
Huh? He left?

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:19.590
Yeah, but we don't know where to.

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:23.090
But it's a big step!
Maybe he's meeting someone?

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.810
Oh! Maybe the guys that came to visit!

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.760
--Hmm?
--Huh?

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:34.770
I bet he left to see them when they
came to see him! What a tragedy!

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:37.770
They're probably hanging out by now!

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.570
I sure hope so.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:40.940
Mmm.

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.700
Big Bro? Welcome home!

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:17.770
What now, Captain?

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:23.030
He's totally different now.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:24.820
Yeah.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:28.620
When he's like that, he ain't coming back.

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:35.580
If we don't find someone,
we can't play prefecturals.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.170
We need to act quickly.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.380
We sure do.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:05.360
<i>I'm not gonna regret it</i>

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:11.160
<i>I honestly won't</i>

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:18.920
<i>The stairs to that dear future</i>

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:27.050
<i>Are crumbling down</i>

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:31.470
<i>Just who are they</i>

00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:38.940
<i>There's a me just like me at my side</i>

00:22:38.940 --> 00:22:41.940
<i>Laughing</i>

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:49.530
<i>All the many sights and</i>

00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:52.990
<i>All the words you left behind</i>

00:22:52.990 --> 00:22:59.790
<i>Are looking a little warped</i>

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:03.210
<i>Someone, anyone tell me</i>

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:06.170
<i>It hurts, it hurts, it hurts</i>

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:14.510
<i>What am I suddenly crying for?</i>
